## 3. The Ghost Phase Test (Ultimate Kill-Switch)

> **If a system exhibits a macroscopic response (e.g., Meissner effect or zero resistance) while its internal information regime is demonstrably incoherent or insolvent, the SOX framework is falsified.**

The burden of proof lies with the auditor to demonstrate that the observed response corresponds to a stable, extensive phase.

